{"bundle_id":"population.w344-open-problem-p0018-checked-partials-20261010","entries":[{"key":"graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example","logical_id":"math:probability.graph_matrices:graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example","revision":{"assumptions":[],"conditions":[],"disposition_reason":"","domain":"probability theory","evidence_ids":[],"kind":"concept","logical_id":"math:probability.graph_matrices:graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example","metadata":{"draft":"w344/bundle_009.json","proof_text":""},"provenance":{"imported_by":"w344","locator":"urn:mb-local:f530f9044eb0a47f","source_content_digest":"sha256:94e70d58b352408a6c15a740901a27da75507c3443943b90050a51d6db33ecaf","source_id":"owner-w344-open-problems-20261010:graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example","source_revision":"2026-10-10 worker result; source-backed scope correction; independent audit pending w346; novelty unverified","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"trust_class":"curated_secondary"},"schema_version":1,"statement":"Definition 14.2 in the cached Randomstrasse101 paper partitions all shape vertices into left and right sets. The diagonal signed-degree construction using the same vertex on both sides and an unindexed leaf requires a broader graph-matrix convention. Its finite norm experiment therefore supplies no special-case answer under this literal definition. The valid one-edge example uses distinct left and right vertices. Exact indexing conventions must be fixed before assigning shape exponents.","status":"unverified","supersedes":[],"title":"Exclude an overlapping diagonal example from the cited graph-matrix convention"},"revision_digest":"sha256:d79340e1a0adba35c7edbe5c70b36a3f13d4b6e2a9e2c1661a0ed52e6611d275","revision_id":"claim_d79340e1a0adba35c7edbe5c70b36a3f13d4b6e2a9e2c1661a0ed52e6611d275"},{"key":"single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm","logical_id":"math:probability.graph_matrices:single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm","revision":{"assumptions":["Independent Rademacher variables for unordered distinct pairs","Single-edge shape","Injective labels","Disjoint left/right partition"],"conditions":[],"disposition_reason":"","domain":"probability theory","evidence_ids":[],"kind":"lemma","logical_id":"math:probability.graph_matrices:single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm","metadata":{"draft":"w344/bundle_009.json","proof_text":"Randomstrasse101, arXiv:2603.29571, Definition 14.2 and Conjecture 31, PDF p.14, define the cited restricted graph matrices using a partition into left and right vertex sets. Overlapping index vertices and unindexed internal vertices are not supplied by that displayed definition. The diagonal signed-degree experiment in special_case_measurements.jsonl therefore belongs to a broader convention and is explicitly excluded as a special case of this literal problem. Its finite calculations are retained only as a scope warning.

A valid shape has two distinct vertices u,v, one edge uv, U={u} and V={v}. Injective labeling gives an n by n symmetric Rademacher matrix A with zero diagonal. It satisfies E||A||=Theta(sqrt(n)), so f=1/2 and g=0 for this shape. The lower bound is deterministic: ||A||>=||A||_F/sqrt(n)=sqrt(n-1). For a fixed unit real x, x^T A x=sum_(i<j)2x_i x_j epsilon_ij. Its moment-generating function is at most exp(s^2), since cosh z<=exp(z^2/2) and sum_(i<j)x_i^2 x_j^2<=1/2. Hence P(|x^T A x|>=r)<=2 exp(-r^2/4). A 1/4 net of the unit sphere has at most 9^n points and ||A||<=2 max_net |x^T A x|; a union bound and integration of this tail give E||A||<=C sqrt(n). This proves the shape exponents, without resolving the all-shapes existence conjecture.

valid_shape_measurements.json uses 12 samples each at n=64,128,256 and verifies the shape's n(n-1) nonzero entries. The mean norm divided by sqrt(n) is 1.926,1.955,1.974. At n=256 the old Frobenius upper bound is 255.500 and the mean norm is 31.5894, a factor 8.088 numerical gap. The experiment illustrates the bound's loss; the proved improvement is the order n to order sqrt(n) for this one shape."},"provenance":{"imported_by":"w344","locator":"urn:mb-local:f530f9044eb0a47f","source_content_digest":"sha256:14a6211717a4feb7696df4033fa9c157f73f05c7fe9adbdf04eab08c315bbd9f","source_id":"owner-w344-open-problems-20261010:single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm","source_revision":"2026-10-10 worker result; proof; independent audit pending w346; novelty unverified","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"trust_class":"curated_secondary"},"schema_version":1,"statement":"Under the partition convention of Randomstrasse101 Definition 14.2, the shape with one edge uv, U={u} and V={v}, gives a symmetric n by n Rademacher matrix A with zero diagonal. Its expected operator norm is Theta(sqrt(n)), so this shape has exponents f=1/2 and g=0. Deterministically ||A||>=sqrt(n-1) by its Frobenius norm. For each unit real x, P(|x^T A x|>=r)<=2exp(-r^2/4); a 1/4 sphere net of size at most 9^n and integration give the O(sqrt(n)) expectation bound. This does not resolve the existence conjecture for every fixed shape.","status":"unverified","supersedes":[],"title":"Sharp expected norm for the valid single-edge graph-matrix shape"},"revision_digest":"sha256:c31e18510c0b2b56764891bba3785f18638d4ceab8ead33f5700c14af007c2ea","revision_id":"claim_c31e18510c0b2b56764891bba3785f18638d4ceab8ead33f5700c14af007c2ea"}],"metadata":{"author_agent":"w344","draft_file":"w344/bundle_009.json","verification_disposition":"population-phase content, trust CURATED_SECONDARY, pending QA"},"relations":[{"kind":"cites","metadata":{},"rationale":"New end: "Definition 14.2 in the cached Randomstrasse101 paper partitions all shape vertices into left and right sets. The diagonal"; existing end: "For each fixed graph shape alpha with specified left and right index sets, form M_alpha by summing injective". This result addresses or audits P0018; the cited card identifies its mathematical context and is not used as a proof or a current openness certificate.","source":{"scope":"bundle_entry","value":"graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example"},"target":{"scope":"existing_node","value":"claim_33f97b51ed6596472f904cbd29b410358bbddb29a1513f2cf88bf9eaf2c84199"},"weight":1.0},{"kind":"specializes","metadata":{},"rationale":"New end: "Under the partition convention of Randomstrasse101 Definition 14.2, the shape with one edge uv, U={u} and V={v}, gives"; existing end: "For each fixed graph shape alpha with specified left and right index sets, form M_alpha by summing injective". This result addresses or audits P0018; the cited card identifies its mathematical context and is not used as a proof or a current openness certificate.","source":{"scope":"bundle_entry","value":"single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm"},"target":{"scope":"existing_node","value":"claim_33f97b51ed6596472f904cbd29b410358bbddb29a1513f2cf88bf9eaf2c84199"},"weight":1.0}],"release_manifest":{"approved_by":"population-gate claude-mathbrain-build-0802","authorization_key_id":"population-gate-20260802","authorization_mac":"hmac-sha256:81215347e3af8f7a83a3dfa1eef2d8e1ed35f1c5085e6cc8af9880824858a3f5","claim_bindings":[{"entry_key":"graph-matrix-partition-convention-excludes-diagonal-internal-vertex-example","proof_digest":null,"proof_locator":null,"source_artifact_ids":["91f5b7cb681cca6733f6262e103a3afc"],"statement_digest":"sha256:79698246479c605a6e354a24f1008273ce87ec48ff49c9aead062e751445c56b","statement_locator":"urn:mb-local:f530f9044eb0a47f"},{"entry_key":"single-edge-partition-graph-matrix-sharp-norm","proof_digest":"sha256:6d97f04df8eeec0ef83d4abc58077c1e5b5f9014e0bf94d6e0a8ad80